== White Candy Modeling Chocolate ==

Melt @white candy melts{16%oz} in a #plastic or microwave-safe bowl{} in the
#microwave{} or stove-top #sauce pan{}.

Warm @corn syrup{4%oz}(warmed for a few seconds until about body temperature)
and add @gel food coloring{few drops}.

> Remember that your final product will be lighter than the color of your corn
> syrup. You can also add color later if you want.

Fold mixture together with a #spatula{} until mixture starts to seize and
resembles soft serve ice cream.

> It is important to not over-mix or your modeling chocolate will get oily.

Wrap in #plastic wrap{} and let set until chocolate is firm but still pliable.
Usually ~{2%hours} depending on how hot it is in your room.

Unwrap chocolate and knead until smooth, smashing any hard lumps with your
fingers.

Re-wrap chocolate and place back in plastic wrap to set up until hard.

== Chocolate Modeling Chocolate ==

Melt @chocolate{16%oz}(any kind) in a plastic or microwave-safe bowl in the
microwave or stove-top sauce pan.

Warm @corn syrup{6%oz} and add @?gel food coloring{few drops} if desired.

Fold mixture together with a spatula until mixture starts to seize and
resembles soft serve ice cream.

> It is important to not over-mix or your modeling chocolate will get oily.

Wrap in plastic wrap and let set until chocolate is firm but still pliable.
Usually ~{2%hours} depending on how hot it is in your room.

Unwrap chocolate and knead until smooth, smashing any hard lumps with your
fingers.

Re-wrap chocolate and place back in plastic wrap to set up until hard.